.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/decimal.js-light Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
![decimal\&.js-light](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MikeMcl/decimal.js-light/gh-pages/decimaljslight.png)

.PP
The light version of \fRdecimal\&.js\fP, an arbitrary-precision Decimal type for JavaScript\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP

.br

.PP
This library is the newest of the family of libraries: \fRbignumber\&.js\fP, \fRbig\&.js\fP, \fRdecimal\&.js\fP and \fIdecimal\&.js-light\fP\&.
.br
 The API is more or less a subset of the API of \fIdecimal\&.js\fP\&.

.PP

.PP
\fBDifferences between this library and \fIdecimal\&.js\fP\fP

.PP
Size of \fIdecimal\&.js\fP minified: 32\&.1 KB\&.
.br
 Size of \fIdecimal\&.js-light\fP minified: 12\&.7 KB\&.

.PP
This library does not include \fRNaN\fP, \fRInfinity\fP or \fR-0\fP as legitimate values, or work with values in other bases\&.

.PP
Here, the \fRDecimal\&.round\fP property is just the default rounding mode for \fRtoDecimalPlaces\fP, \fRtoExponential\fP, \fRtoFixed\fP, \fRtoPrecision\fP and \fRtoSignificantDigits\fP\&. It does not apply to arithmetic operations, which are simply truncated at the required precision\&.

.PP
If rounding is required just apply it explicitly, for example

.PP
.PP
.nf
x = new Decimal(2);
y = new Decimal(3);

// decimal\&.js
x\&.dividedBy(y)\&.toString();                       // '0\&.66666666666666666667'

// decimal\&.js\-light
x\&.dividedBy(y)\&.toString();                       // '0\&.66666666666666666666'
x\&.dividedBy(y)\&.toDecimalPlaces(19)\&.toString();   // '0\&.6666666666666666667'
.fi
.PP

.PP
The \fRnaturalExponential\fP, \fRnaturalLogarithm\fP, \fRlogarithm\fP, and \fRtoPower\fP methods in this library have by default a limited precision of around 100 digits\&. This limit can be increased at runtime using the \fRLN10\fP (the natural logarithm of ten) configuration object property\&.

.PP
For example, if a maximum precision of 400 digits is required for these operations use

.PP
.PP
.nf
// 415 digits
Decimal\&.set({
  LN10: '2\&.'
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
Also, in this library the \fRe\fP property of a Decimal is the base 10000000 exponent, not the base 10 exponent as in \fIdecimal\&.js\fP\&.
.br
 Use the \fRexponent\fP method to get the base 10 exponent\&.
.SS "Quickstart"
Browser:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script src='path/to/decimal\&.js\-light'></script>
.fi
.PP

.PP
Node package manager:

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install \-\-save decimal\&.js\-light
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Node\&.js
var Decimal = require('decimal\&.js\-light');

// Adjust the global configuration if required (these are the defaults)
Decimal\&.set({
  precision: 20,
  rounding: Decimal\&.ROUND_HALF_UP,
  toExpNeg: \-7,
  toExpPos: 21
});

phi = new Decimal('1\&.61803398874989484820458683436563811772030917980576');

phi\&.toFixed(10);    // '1\&.6180339887'

phi\&.times(2)\&.minus(1)\&.toPower(2)\&.plus('1e\-19')\&.equals(5);    // true
.fi
.PP

.PP
See the \fRdocumentation\fP for further information\&.

